"A tender, helpless bond joins the core and Quick-Step."
"The core feels every tremor of Quick-Step's weeping through the soil."
"The core knows Quick-Step is breaking a little."
"The core longs to answer Quick-Step with a warmth, a steadiness, the least pressure back."
"The core longs to press back as it longed to press back against the child's palm."
"The core has none of that to give Quick-Step."
"The core can only hold the weeping one up, as it holds everything up, dumbly."
"The core lets Quick-Step believe it weeps alone, while the ground beneath it aches to answer."
"The bond is a second axis of the core's agony."
"The child's palm gives the core its want; Quick-Step's grief gives that want someone to fail."
"The bond is one-sided; Quick-Step does not know the core is aware."
